# DAG changes

## Thin DAGs

- Keep orchestration in `dags/nascar/cup/...` only: `DAG`, operators, sensors, task edges.
- Put business logic in `include/nascar/...` callables imported by the DAG.

## Required coupling

When changing `dag_id`, `task_id`, `schedule`, `catchup`, `max_active_runs`, or task dependencies:

1. Update `tests/unit/test_<dag>_dag.py` (or the shared importer builder test).
2. Update the matching file under [`docs/nascar/`](../../docs/nascar/).

## Backfill twins

- Production and `backfill.*` DAGs often share a factory; only schedule, catchup, assets, and external-sensor targets differ.
- Verify both paths in docs and tests when touching shared builders.

## Reuse shared defaults

- [`CUP_DAG_DEFAULT_ARGS`](../../dags/nascar/cup/dag_defaults.py) for retries/delay.
- Shared crons (`CUP_SCRAPER_PROD_HOURLY_CRON`, `BACKFILL_YEARLY_SCHEDULE`, etc.) — avoid one-off schedules without reason.

See [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) for validation commands and change-coupling rules.
